{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 23:02:40", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-bb20619e-40b6-4915-8a18-d0c40155680c', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 2: Enhanced Task Monitoring",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/architecture_m2.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/milestone_plan.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/frontend_tasks_m2.md",\n  "project_id": "6d9cbb19",\n  "milestone_id": "m2"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018Ybm5Ssppb3aD2FjsDNGMX', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/architecture_m2.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018Ybm5Ssppb3aD2FjsDNGMX', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Milestone 2 Architecture\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Purpose\\nDevelop an intelligent task monitoring system that provides real-time, visually intuitive tracking of agent tasks within the ensemble project management workflow.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\nAdopted a modular, event-driven design with separation of concerns:\\n- Data Parsing Layer: Responsible for reading and interpreting project state\\n- Display Layer: Handles formatting and rendering of task information\\n- Update Mechanism: Manages real-time synchronization\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Languages and Frameworks\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n  - Rationale: Strong typing, excellent file/JSON parsing, cross-platform compatibility\\n  - Alternatives Considered: Bash scripting (too limited), Node.js (unnecessary complexity)\\n\\n### Key Libraries\\n- `json`: Native JSON parsing\\n- `rich`: Advanced terminal formatting and color support\\n- `watchdog`: File system monitoring for real-time updates\\n- `colorama`: Cross-platform terminal color support\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. Task Parser (`task_parser.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Read project tracking JSON from `~/.ensemble/projects/`\\n- Parse and validate task metadata\\n- Extract task status, progress, and details\\n\\n**Input**: Project JSON file\\n**Output**: Structured task data\\n\\n### 2. Display Formatter (`display_manager.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Convert parsed tasks to human-readable format\\n- Apply color coding and status icons\\n- Generate task summary statistics\\n\\n**Features**:\\n- Status icon mapping: \\n  - \\u2705 Completed tasks\\n  - \\u26a1 In-progress tasks\\n  - \\u23f3 Pending tasks\\n  - \\u274c Blocked tasks\\n\\n### 3. Update Watcher (`file_watcher.py`)\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Monitor project tracking file for changes\\n- Trigger task list refresh\\n- Handle file access errors gracefully\\n\\n## D. Data Flow Diagram\\n```\\n[Project JSON] \\u2192 [Task Parser] \\u2192 [Validation] \\u2192 [Display Formatter] \\u2192 [Terminal Display]\\n                      \\u2191                               \\u2193\\n               [File Watcher] \\u2190----------- [Periodic Refresh]\\n```\\n\\n## E. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\ntmux_monitoring_dashboard/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 scripts/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 monitoring/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 task_watcher.py        # Main script\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 task_parser.py          # JSON parsing logic\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 display_manager.py      # Formatting and display\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 file_watcher.py         # Real-time update mechanism\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 requirements.txt                # Python dependencies\\n```\\n\\n## F. Error Handling Strategy\\n- Graceful handling of missing/malformed project files\\n- Configurable logging for debugging\\n- Fallback display for incomplete data\\n- Retry mechanisms for file access issues\\n\\n## G. Performance Considerations\\n- Lightweight parsing (minimal CPU usage)\\n- Efficient file watching\\n- Update interval: 1-2 seconds\\n- Minimal memory footprint\\n\\n## H. Deployment Approach\\n- Callable as standalone Python script\\n- Embeddable in tmux dashboard\\n- Cross-platform compatibility (macOS, Linux)\\n\\n## I. Testing Strategy\\n1. Unit Tests\\n   - Task parsing accuracy\\n   - Display formatting\\n   - Error handling scenarios\\n\\n2. Integration Tests\\n   - File watching reliability\\n   - Real-time update performance\\n   - Tmux integration\\n\\n## J. Open Questions / User Input Needed\\n- Preferred update interval (currently 1-2 seconds)\\n- Desired level of task detail in display\\n- Custom color scheme preferences\\n\\n## K. Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Risk**: Inconsistent project file format\\n   **Mitigation**: Robust schema validation, default values\\n\\n2. **Risk**: Performance overhead\\n   **Mitigation**: Efficient parsing, minimal background processing\\n\\n3. **Risk**: Cross-platform compatibility\\n   **Mitigation**: Extensive testing, use of cross-platform libraries"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01A4BPGRBG9HwiR9jupoazGU', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01A4BPGRBG9HwiR9jupoazGU', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nCreating a tmux-based 2x2 monitoring dashboard that provides real-time visibility into the ensemble agent swarm\'s operation, allowing developers to observe agent activity, browse output files, and track task progress in a single terminal view.\\n\\n## Milestone Breakdown\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Basic Tmux Layout (MVP)\\n**Objective**: Create a functional 2x2 tmux layout with basic monitoring capabilities\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `scripts/deployment/start_monitor.sh` - Main script to launch tmux dashboard\\n- `scripts/deployment/stop_monitor.sh` - Script to cleanly stop the dashboard  \\n- Basic 2x2 tmux layout with:\\n  - Pane 1 (top-left): Shell ready for CLI interaction\\n  - Pane 2 (top-right): Live tail of backend.log\\n  - Pane 3 (bottom-left): Vim opened to output directory\\n  - Pane 4 (bottom-right): Basic watch command on project file\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Single command launches complete dashboard\\n- All 4 panes display correctly in 2x2 grid\\n- Log streaming works in real-time\\n- File browser navigates output directory\\n- Session persists if terminal disconnects\\n- Clean shutdown script works\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Estimated Effort**: Medium\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Enhanced Task Monitoring  \\n**Objective**: Create intelligent task watcher with formatted display and real-time updates\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `scripts/monitoring/task_watcher.py` - Python script to parse project.json and display formatted task list\\n- Enhanced task display with:\\n  - Status icons (\\u2705 \\u26a1 \\u23f3) for completed, in-progress, pending\\n  - Task count summary\\n  - Auto-refresh capability\\n  - Clean formatting\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Task status updates in real-time as agents work\\n- Clear visual distinction between task states\\n- Summary count shows overall progress\\n- Performance is responsive (updates every 1-2 seconds)\\n- Handles missing/malformed project files gracefully\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\\n\\n**Estimated Effort**: Medium\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Full CLI Integration and Polish\\n**Objective**: Complete integration with Claude CLI and production-ready polish\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- Full Claude CLI integration in Pane 1\\n- Enhanced log formatting/filtering for Pane 2\\n- Configuration options for customization\\n- Complete documentation and usage examples\\n- Error handling and edge case management\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Claude CLI runs automatically in Pane 1 with proper setup\\n- Log display is clean and informative\\n- User can customize session name, directories, project ID\\n- Documentation covers all features and troubleshooting\\n- Works reliably across macOS and Linux with tmux 3.0+\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 complete\\n\\n**Estimated Effort**: Medium\\n\\n## Timeline Summary\\n- **Milestone 1**: Foundation (Basic tmux layout with monitoring)\\n- **Milestone 2**: Intelligence (Smart task tracking)  \\n- **Milestone 3**: Integration (Production-ready with CLI)\\n\\n## Technical Strategy\\n1. Start with shell scripts for rapid prototyping\\n2. Use Python for task parsing and formatting logic\\n3. Leverage existing project tracking system at ~/.ensemble/projects/\\n4. Build incrementally - each milestone is independently valuable\\n5. Focus on reliability and user experience\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n- Test across different tmux versions and shell environments\\n- Handle edge cases like missing files, permission issues\\n- Provide clear error messages and troubleshooting guidance\\n- Keep dependencies minimal (standard tools: tmux, vim, python, bash)"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01R52ziwRat6RCkANEChH6QH', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Enhanced Task Monitoring', 'description': 'Frontend tasks for real-time task monitoring dashboard with formatted display and auto-refresh'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01R52ziwRat6RCkANEChH6QH', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "299a6d4b", "message": "Created project: Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Enhanced Task Monitoring", "summary": {"project_id": "299a6d4b", "project_name": "Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Enhanced Task Monitoring", "description": "Frontend tasks for real-time task monitoring dashboard with formatted display and auto-refresh", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T23:02:21.115351", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T23:02:21.115351", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T23:02:21.115351", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Enhanced Task Monitoring\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01X7yDH81oUkjUFXytYW1FxQ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/frontend_tasks_m2.md', 'content': '# Frontend Tasks - Tmux Monitoring Dashboard (Milestone 2)\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone focuses on developing a real-time, intelligent task monitoring system with visually formatted display and auto-refresh capabilities.\n\n## Key Components\n1. Task Parsing Service\n2. Display Formatter\n3. Real-time Update Mechanism\n4. Error Handling Layer\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### 1. Task Parsing Service\n- **Task Name**: Create Task Parsing Utility\n- **Description**: Develop Python utility to parse project tracking JSON files\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Reads JSON from `~/.ensemble/projects/`\n  - Extracts task metadata reliably\n  - Handles missing/malformed files gracefully\n- **Dependencies**: None\n- **Complexity**: Medium\n\n### 2. Status Icon Mapping\n- **Task Name**: Implement Status Icon System\n- **Description**: Create mapping for task status icons and colors\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - \\u2705 for Completed tasks (green)\n  - \\u26a1 for In-Progress tasks (blue)\n  - \\u23f3 for Pending tasks (yellow)\n  - \\u274c for Blocked tasks (red)\n- **Dependencies**: \n  - Task Parsing Service\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n\n### 3. Display Formatter\n- **Task Name**: Build Task Display Logic\n- **Description**: Convert parsed tasks to human-readable, color-coded format\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Generate task list with icons\n  - Show task count summary\n  - Apply consistent color scheme\n  - Format for clear terminal display\n- **Dependencies**:\n  - Task Parsing Service\n  - Status Icon Mapping\n- **Complexity**: Medium\n\n### 4. File Watcher Module\n- **Task Name**: Implement Real-time Update Mechanism\n- **Description**: Create file watching utility for automatic task list refresh\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Monitor project JSON for changes\n  - Trigger refresh every 1-2 seconds\n  - Minimal CPU/memory usage\n  - Graceful error handling\n- **Dependencies**:\n  - Task Parsing Service\n  - Display Formatter\n- **Complexity**: Complex\n\n### 5. Error Handling Layer\n- **Task Name**: Robust Error Management\n- **Description**: Implement comprehensive error handling for file access and parsing\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Detect and log file read errors\n  - Provide fallback display for incomplete data\n  - Show user-friendly error messages\n  - Prevent application crash on file issues\n- **Dependencies**:\n  - All previous components\n- **Complexity**: Medium\n\n### 6. Performance Optimization\n- **Task Name**: Performance Tuning\n- **Description**: Optimize parsing and display refresh\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Update interval under 2 seconds\n  - Low memory footprint\n  - Responsive UI\n- **Dependencies**:\n  - All previous components\n- **Complexity**: Complex\n\n## Task Dependencies Graph\n```\n[Task Parsing Service] → [Status Icon Mapping]\n                        ↘\n[Display Formatter] ← [File Watcher Module]\n        ↓\n[Error Handling Layer]\n        ↓\n[Performance Optimization]\n```\n\n## Technical Notes\n- **Framework**: Pure Python\n- **Libraries**: \n  - `json` for parsing\n  - `rich` for formatting\n  - `watchdog` for file monitoring\n- **Target Environment**: Terminal/tmux\n- **Performance Target**: <2s refresh, <50MB memory\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n1. Inconsistent project file format\n   - Mitigation: Robust schema validation\n2. Performance overhead\n   - Mitigation: Efficient parsing, minimal processing\n3. Cross-platform compatibility\n   - Mitigation: Test on macOS and Linux'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01X7yDH81oUkjUFXytYW1FxQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/frontend_tasks_m2.md", "backup_path": null, "was_overwrite": false}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 98.2%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.3\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['f